<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE sailpoint PUBLIC "sailpoint.dtd" "sailpoint.dtd">
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  Which IIQ node runs which background service.

  Two nodes share the database (docker-compose.yml: "iiq" and
  "iiq-batch"). The stock definitions carry hosts="global", i.e. every
  node starts a Task scheduler and a Request processor. Restricting both
  to the batch node gives the usual production shape: the UI node only
  serves requests, tasks and requests run on exactly one JVM, and there
  is exactly one Quartz scheduler (IIQ does not configure Quartz
  clustering; the hosts list is the mechanism that keeps schedulers
  apart).

  hosts= is a comma-separated list of Server names, i.e. the values of
  -Diiq.hostname (IIQ_BATCH_NODE in .env). Rename both or neither. The
  same effect can be reached per node in the UI (Global Settings >
  Servers, which writes includedServices/excludedServices on the Server
  object); a file is what survives a volume reset.

  BundleProfileRelation (the role/profile relation synchronizer, 8.4+) is
  pinned as well: a periodic database job that coordinates through a lock
  (lockTimeout), so two nodes would only take turns doing the same work.
  Its attributes are copied from init.xml - a full object replaces them.

  Note on "Request": IIQ starts the RequestProcessor thread on EVERY node
  regardless of hosts= (Servicer skips the host check for this one
  service), because some requests are addressed to a specific host, e.g.
  terminating a task that runs there. The About page therefore shows
  "Request Scheduler Status: Started" on the UI node too. Unaddressed
  requests are still taken only by hosts in this list
  (ServicerUtil.isServiceAllowedOnServer in RequestProcessor).

  Full objects, not a merge: the stock Task and Request definitions have
  no attributes besides the description, so nothing is lost. Every other
  service (Heartbeat, Monitoring, PluginSync, FullText, ...) keeps
  hosts=global.
  ===========================================================================
-->
<sailpoint>

  <ServiceDefinition name="Task" hosts="iiq-batch">
    <Description>
Service definition for the Task scheduler service.
    </Description>
  </ServiceDefinition>

  <ServiceDefinition name="Request" hosts="iiq-batch">
    <Description>
Service definition for the Request processor service.
    </Description>
  </ServiceDefinition>

  <ServiceDefinition name="BundleProfileRelation" hosts="iiq-batch" interval="60">
    <Description>
      Service definition for the BundleProfileRelationService.
    </Description>
    <Attributes>
      <Map>
        <entry key="lockTimeout">
          <value>
            <Integer>300</Integer>
          </value>
        </entry>
        <entry key="cycleSeconds">
          <value>
            <Integer>10</Integer>
          </value>
        </entry>
      </Map>
    </Attributes>
  </ServiceDefinition>

</sailpoint>
